@*
    A page that exists to come out of a printer.

    Not the back-office layout with things hidden: no sidebar, no navigation, no
    Bootstrap. A print stylesheet bolted onto the admin shell would still load
    the shell, and every future change to the sidebar would be one more thing
    that could push the invoice onto a second page. This document has no chrome
    to hide because none was ever added.

    Its only screen affordance is the toolbar at the top, which is itself hidden
    when printing.
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>@ViewData["Title"]</title>

    <link rel="icon" href="~/favicon.ico" sizes="any" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/print.css" asp-append-version="true" />

    @* A printed document is not a page anyone should find in a search engine,
       and these URLs carry a customer's address. *@
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow" />
</head>
<body>
@RenderBody()
@await RenderSectionAsync("Scripts", required: false)
</body>
</html>
